# Shift rules

- Jalali calendar; official holidays in `holidays.js` (`IRAN_HOLIDAYS` 1403–1405).
- Week starts **Friday**. Weekly rotation: one week morning/night, next week swapped.
- Default **period mode**: 21st of month → 20th of next month (`PERIOD_START_DAY = 21`).
- Saturday & Friday: morning person OFF; night still works.
- Official + company holidays: morning OFF only; night works; compensatory OFF later on a morning day. Compensatory cells are **blank**, not labeled «جبرانی شب».
- Company Thursday holidays: admin ticks in UI.
- Monthly quotas: user enters normal OFF count + Thursday OFF count (optional per person).
- Cell labels: **صبح / شب / خالی**. No «OFF» text in boxes.
- Manual cell dropdown (صبح / شب / خالی): **admin only**. Viewers cannot edit.
- Hardcoded Hamed overrides in `app.js`: OFF on 29 Mordad and 9 Shahrivar 1405; work (not OFF) on 25–26 Mordad; OFF moved from 22 to 29 Mordad.
- End report: day shifts, Thursdays worked, OFFs, Friday/official holidays.
- Export: CSV, horizontal Excel, continue pattern, until end of 1405.
